# Standard JavaScript Error Types 💥

JavaScript has built-in error classes that tell you exactly what went wrong:

| Error Type | Cause | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `ReferenceError` | Accessing an undeclared variable | `console.log(unknownVar)` |
| `TypeError` | Performing an invalid operation on a type | `null.toUpperCase()` or `5()` |
| `SyntaxError` | Code violates JavaScript grammar | `let x = ;` |
| `RangeError` | Numeric value is out of allowable range | `new Array(-1)` |
| `URIError` | Malformed URI in `decodeURI()` | `decodeURI('%')` |

