# The `finally` Block 🧹

The `finally` block **always executes**, regardless of whether an error was thrown or not! Perfect for closing file handles, stopping loaders, or freeing memory:

```javascript
let isLoading = true;

try {
  console.log("Performing operation...");
  throw new Error("Disk full");
} catch (err) {
  console.log("Handled error:", err.message);
} finally {
  isLoading = false; // Guaranteed to run!
  console.log("Loader stopped. isLoading =", isLoading);
}
```

