# Throwing Errors (`throw`) 🚨

Use the `throw` statement to signal an exceptional condition:

```javascript
function withdrawMoney(accountBalance, amount) {
  if (typeof amount !== "number" || amount <= 0) {
    throw new TypeError("Withdrawal amount must be a positive number.");
  }
  if (amount > accountBalance) {
    throw new RangeError("Insufficient funds for this withdrawal.");
  }
  return accountBalance - amount;
}

try {
  withdrawMoney(100, 150);
} catch (err) {
  console.error(`[${err.name}]: ${err.message}`);
}
```

