# Creating Custom Error Classes 🏷️

Create application-specific error types by extending the built-in `Error` class:

```javascript
class ValidationError extends Error {
  constructor(message, field) {
    super(message);
    this.name = "ValidationError";
    this.field = field;
  }
}

try {
  throw new ValidationError("Email format is invalid", "userEmail");
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof ValidationError) {
    console.log(`Validation failed on field '${err.field}': ${err.message}`);
  }
}
```

