# Re-throwing Unhandled Errors 🤾

Only catch errors you know how to handle. If you encounter an unexpected error, re-throw it so higher-level handlers can manage it:

```javascript
function readConfig(jsonString) {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(jsonString);
  } catch (err) {
    if (err instanceof SyntaxError) {
      console.warn("Invalid config syntax, returning default config.");
      return { theme: "default" };
    }
    // Re-throw unknown errors!
    throw err;
  }
}

console.log(readConfig("{ bad json }"));
```

