# Error Causation & Chaining (`Error.cause`) 🔗

Modern JavaScript allows attaching a `cause` property to preserve the original root error while providing a user-friendly wrapper:

```javascript
try {
  try {
    JSON.parse("invalid");
  } catch (lowLevelError) {
    throw new Error("Failed to load user configuration", { cause: lowLevelError });
  }
} catch (wrappedError) {
  console.log("High-level message:", wrappedError.message);
  console.log("Original root cause:", wrappedError.cause.message);
}
```

