# Advanced Console Debugging Tools 🧰

Beyond `console.log`, the `console` object provides powerful inspection methods:

```javascript
// 1. console.table: Formats arrays of objects into a table!
const users = [
  { id: 1, name: "Alice", role: "Admin" },
  { id: 2, name: "Bob", role: "Editor" }
];
console.table(users);

// 2. console.time & console.timeEnd: Measures execution time!
console.time("Array Operation");
let arr = Array.from({ length: 10000 }, (_, i) => i * 2);
console.timeEnd("Array Operation");
```

