# `console.assert` & `console.trace` 🕵️

## 1. `console.assert(condition, message)`:
Logs an error message **only if the condition is false**:
```javascript
const userAge = 15;
console.assert(userAge >= 18, "Validation Warning: User is underage!");
```

## 2. `console.trace()`:
Prints a full stack trace showing the exact execution path and function calls that led to that moment:
```javascript
function stepA() { stepB(); }
function stepB() { console.trace("Trace stack history"); }
stepA();
```

